video
 * drv3DfxVoodooVSA - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvATIMach64
 * drvATIRage
 * drvCirrusLogicGD5434 - builds and links against the reference binary, 19/21 functions byte-identical, apple-generic version bundle present, SGS VERS_STRING/VERS_NUM unmet, setMode: and setPCIConfiguration unmatched; not hardware-tested
 * drvIBMThinkPad760EDDisplay - reconstructed against the reference binary, built, ledger advanced; not hardware-tested
 * drvMatroxMGA - complete
 * drvNVidiaRiva - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvS3Generic - complete
 * drvVBE20DisplayDriver - reconstructed against Apple's VBE20DisplayDriver_reloc from OPENSTEP 4.2 User Patch 4, the only driver in the tree reconstructed against a different OS release; 15 partition entries, 13 hand-written and all 13 byte-identical in place, __cstring and __data byte-identical, whole __text differs in 3 raw bytes, all in the two build-generated Kernel Server methods (the _VBE20DisplayDriver_instance common the reference leaves unallocated, and IO_DRIVERKIT_VERSION 420 there against 500 here); builds and links. Boot gate passed 2026-09-22 against the kernel that exports _VBEModeInfo2IODisplayInfo (spec 2): sarld links it as a Boot Driver, it takes the "card not in VBE mode" path and registers as VBEDisplay0, and no other boot driver is lost; a kernel without the symbol fails its link with "rld(): Undefined symbols" as predicted (docs/kernel/i386-vbe-console.md). The framebuffer path waits on the booter; not hardware-tested
 * drvVBoxVideo - complete
 * drvVGA - both halves reconstructed against Apple's binaries; VGA_reloc 29 of 38 ledger entries assembly-matched with 6 control-flow-confirmed, VGA_psdrvr 34 of 53 with the other 19 linker and dyld glue; emu486 is hand-written assembly, transcribed rather than decompiled, and assembles to the reference's exact 10496 bytes with every differing byte an address field off by a constant link displacement. Builds clean, no missing strings or symbols either half, every section matching bar __TEXT,__const's build-generated version strings. Boot-tested 2026-09-20 with the rebuilt kernel, which the stock one blocks by dying in the open EIDE defect first: registers VGADisplay0, sets the VGA mode from Default.table and the VESA mode from SVGABIOS.table with the emulator driving a real-mode INT 10h, renders the GUI at 800x600 in 2bpp and round-trips the cursor pixel-exactly over 110 motion events. Reaches the same desktop as part of a fully reconstructed stack with our kernel, drvPCIBus and drvEISABus, all four binaries hash-verified in place first. Not hardware-tested
 * drvVMWareVideo - complete

other - (these live at src/drvBPF and src/drvPortServer, not under drivers-i386)
 * drvBPF - reconstructed against the reference binary, fixes applied, not yet compiled or tested
 * drvPortServer - reconstructed against the reference binary, five pre-existing compile blockers repaired, fixes applied, not yet compiled or tested
